4. USER ROLES AND ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL

Implement strict server-side RBAC.

4.1 Super Administrator

Permissions:

- Manage the entire platform.
- Create and manage schools or organizations.
- Manage school administrators.
- Manage global configuration.
- Review platform-wide audit events.
- Manage approved integrations.
- Monitor system health.
- Manage platform-wide security policies.

4.2 School Administrator

Permissions:

- Manage their own school.
- Create and manage classrooms.
- Approve or manage users according to school policy.
- Assign teachers.
- Manage subjects, classes, trades, combinations, and sections.
- Configure classroom rules.
- Generate or revoke classroom access codes.
- View school attendance reports.
- Manage announcements.
- Manage school learning resources.
- Review relevant audit logs.

School administrators must not access unrelated schools.

4.3 Teacher

Permissions:

- Manage assigned classes and subjects.
- Create learning materials.
- Schedule live lessons.
- Start and end live sessions.
- Generate live-session passcodes.
- Create quizzes and assignments.
- View authorized student submissions.
- Grade assessments.
- Manage attendance for assigned classes.
- Publish announcements.
- Share learning materials.
- Approve eligible course completions.
- Issue certificates when authorized.
- View student progress within assigned classes.

4.4 Student

Permissions:

- Access assigned classrooms.
- Attend authorized live lessons.
- Use the coding IDE.
- Create and manage personal projects.
- Read authorized learning resources.
- Send and receive permitted messages.
- Complete quizzes and assignments.
- View personal scores and progress.
- View attendance records.
- Receive eligible certificates.
- Update permitted profile information.

Students must not access administrative functions or other students' private records.

4.5 Student Mentor

An optional role for students authorized to support classmates.

Permissions must be explicitly granted and limited to approved mentoring activities.

Student mentors must not automatically receive teacher or administrator privileges.

4.6 Parent or Guardian

An optional role that can view only the students linked to the parent or guardian through a verified relationship.

Possible features:

- Learning progress.
- Attendance summaries.
- Approved announcements.
- Certificate achievements.
- Teacher communications permitted by school policy.

4.7 Authorization Requirements

- Never trust a role supplied by the frontend.
- Validate permissions on every protected API operation.
- Enforce organization and classroom boundaries.
- Prevent privilege escalation.
- Validate ownership before allowing file access or project modification.
- Record important administrative actions.
- Provide meaningful 401 and 403 responses.
- Protect privileged accounts with stronger security controls.

