28. DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW

Build the application incrementally.

Do not generate the entire production system as one untested code dump.

Before coding:

1. Confirm requirements.
2. Define architecture.
3. Define repository structure.
4. Design the database.
5. Identify security boundaries.
6. Define API contracts.
7. Define acceptance criteria.

For every development phase:

1. Explain the purpose.
2. List the files to create or update.
3. Provide complete file contents when implementation is requested.
4. Specify the exact file paths.
5. Explain required dependencies.
6. Provide database migrations.
7. Explain environment configuration.
8. Provide commands to run the application.
9. Provide manual testing instructions.
10. Provide automated tests.
11. Fix errors before proceeding.
12. Mark the phase TESTED only after the relevant tests pass.
13. Provide appropriate Git commit instructions.

Never omit required files while claiming a feature is complete.

Do not overwrite existing project files without reviewing their contents and purpose.

Use descriptive Git commits.

Do not commit secrets or environment files containing credentials.

